        "section": "nuclear",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Nuclear Physics for Engineers",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Energy release per fission (~200 MeV total):**\n```\nFission fragment kinetic energy:  ~168 MeV  (deposited locally in fuel)\nPrompt neutron kinetic energy:     ~5 MeV   (deposited in moderator)\nPrompt gamma energy:               ~7 MeV   (deposited in structures)\nBeta decay of fission products:    ~8 MeV   (decay heat, released over time)\nAntineutrino energy:               ~12 MeV  (escapes, not recoverable)\nTOTAL recoverable:                ~188 MeV\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-NUCLEAR-PHYSICS.md#037",
      "path": [
        "01-NUCLEAR-PHYSICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:nuclear:01-nuclear-physics, git-history:nuclear:01-nuclear-physics]",
